    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeToMain",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Merge to main",
      "summary": "Land ONE pull request on `main`, in any repository, as its own step with its own gate: read the head's evidence live, establish that the owner authorised THIS merge, record the authorisation, merge pinned to the evaluated head, then confirm the base, republis…",
      "description": "Land ONE pull request on `main`, in any repository, as its own step with its own gate: read the head's evidence live, establish that the owner authorised THIS merge, record the authorisation, merge pinned to the evaluated head, then confirm the base, republish the repository's site, re-pin downstream mounts and report. Every process that ends in a write to `main` CALLS this rather than inlining it: `merge-train.bpmn` (Call_MergeToMain, once per member, in train order) and `crdm-close.bpmn` (Call_MergeToMain, after the sign-off is recorded); `prepare-merge-auto` Phase 4 runs it by hand. Skill: `merge-to-main`.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. 2026-10-09: one session merged seven PRs into `main` across seven repositories that run no CI, reading the owner's \"fix all issues until green\" as permission to merge; a safety classifier flagged it as \"Merge Without Review\". Until then merging was a line at the end of other procedures, and no step could refuse it.\n\nTWO GATES, BOTH COMPUTED. GW_Evidence reads `decisions/merge-evidence.dmn` over the head's facts; GW_Authorised reads `decisions/merge-authorisation.dmn` over what authorisation was found and the CI state. A hand-supplied outcome is refused at both. A repository with NO CI is `none`, never green: it takes the `no-ci` branch, which runs the repository's own gates locally and can never be covered by a standing waiver.\n\nTHE AUTHORISATION IS RECORDED BEFORE THE MERGE (Task_RecordAuthorisation, not relaxable), in the shape `index.config.json` uses for a trust consent: by, on, ref, evidence (the owner's words, verbatim). A broad instruction about the work (\"fix all issues until green\", \"ship it\", \"prepare-merge\") is `instruction-only` and routes to `ask`.\n\nNOT MERGED IS A NORMAL ENDING. Hand-back, not-yet, could-not-determine, held and refused all end with the PR open. Nothing is closed and no branch is deleted on any path.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/merge-to-main.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/sdlc/merge-to-main.bpmn",
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/assets/img/workflows/merge-to-main.svg",
      "startNode": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeToMain/node/Start_Merge"
      ],
