    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/typologies",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "typologies",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "The graph typologies a harness declares it owns, one node per kind, so no central registry names another harness's subgraph types. Loaded across the instances on first use."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/validators",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "validators",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "The validators a harness's code provides, one node each naming the graph typology and $schema family it checks and the Zod export that checks it, joined onto the kinds on first use."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/tools",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "tools",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Tool definitions — themselves nodes in the KG, per the repo taxonomy.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/tool"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/cat-harness",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "cat-harness",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A Subgraph holding a Harness's own parts, such as Skills, Processes and Roles, where one directory holds more than one of them.",
      "conformsTo": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dmn-1.3"
      ],
      "validatorNotApplicable": "it holds several node kinds typed in different places — skills, workflows, roles, actors. `schema` above already says why one pointer here would be a lie of precision, and that applies to a validator with more force: a runnable one would silently grade 51 JSON files against whichever single shape it named. Each family is validated where it is declared."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#graphTypology/skills",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "skills",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A Subgraph of Skills: the instructions an Actor follows to carry out a Task."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#graphTypology/processes",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "processes",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A Subgraph of Processes: BPMN diagrams that coordinate Tasks, and the decision tables their gateways compute from.",
      "conformsTo": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dmn-1.3",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/w3c-xsd11-structures"
      ],
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are `.bpmn` and `.dmn` — XML, counted 2026-09-24 as 77 and 9. A Zod schema parses JSON, so one here would be a category error; `check:workflows`, `xml-comment-check` and `check-process-documentation` grade them instead."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#graphTypology/scenarios",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "scenarios",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A Subgraph of Roles: the responsibilities an Actor takes on, and who takes them on.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/role-graph"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/policies",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "policies",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "W3C ODRL 2.2 policies: which Actor may do which action, scoped by Process, Task and Role constraints. Actions are the folio profile in skills/permissions/permissions.json.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/odrl"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/methodology",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "methodology",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Judgement methodologies, adopted whole and kept independent — parallel ways to reach a decision, selected by context.",
      "conformsTo": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0"
      ],
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are markdown — 12 files, counted 2026-09-24. `check-methodology-evidence` grades what matters about them, which is whether each cited source actually exists in a library."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/docs",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "docs",
      "renderable": true,
      "summary": "Documentation ABOUT the knowledge graph — how the harness works, what its directories hold, how a process runs. Rendered by the plain just-the-docs pipeline. Distinct from `folio`, which is content an author CREATES using the graph; the difference is the SUBJECT, not the format. An L1 library's catalogue is `library/`; a note about it is a `folio`; the page explaining how ingestion works is `docs`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/proposals",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "proposals",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Proposals for the harness's own features — initial analysis, MVP, options — argued before anything is agreed. A sub-graph of `docs`. When the feature ships, its proposal is MOVED to `requirements` and filed against the `Requirement` schema.",
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are markdown pages of argument with no fixed shape; a proposal is judged by the owner, not parsed. What IS checked mechanically is the move out of it: `check:requirements` refuses a slug that sits in both proposals and requirements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/requirements",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "requirements",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "What the harness promises, one document per shipped feature, each carrying a `Requirement` in its front matter. A sub-graph of `docs`. Test runs point at these statements by `req:<slug>#<key>`.",
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are markdown pages whose FRONT MATTER is a `Requirement`. A registry validator parses a JSON node, so one here would be a category error. `check:requirements` extracts the front matter and parses it against the Requirement schema instead, and requires the id to match the file name."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/doc-group",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "doc-group",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A named group of the documentation's own pages — one folder, one heading in the Pages list. A sub-graph of `docs`.",
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are the docs site's markdown pages, judged as `docs` pages are; a group adds a folder, not a shape."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/auto-docs",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "auto-docs",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Derived indexes over the other graphs — one page per auto-doc TYPE crossed with each SUB-GRAPH that type reaches. A sub-graph of `docs`, written by `scripts/gen-auto-docs.ts` and never by hand. Distinct from `docs` itself by the one question that settles the layer: a docs page is re-authored, an index is regenerated.",
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are generated index PAGES — HTML and markdown with no fixed JSON shape — so a registry validator would be a category error, as on `proposals`. What is checked mechanically is the derivation instead: `auto:docs:check` fails on a stale page, and refuses outright when a type collects nothing while its graph's directories hold files, which is a moved source rather than an empty graph (bean `06e3`)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/external-schema",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "external-schema",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "The specifications this instance depends on — one record per specification, pinning the EDITION in use, with the operative terms derived from the corpus rather than hand-listed; and, beside a record, the pinned edition's own codes where something resolves against them.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/external-schema"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/code-list",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "code-list",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Closed sets of codes — adjudication answers, the namespaces this project mints — one file per list, every code carrying its definition and source, published as SKOS.",
      "validatorRef": "schemas/library/code-list.ts#CodeListSchema"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/vocab-mapping",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "vocab-mapping",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Vocabulary mappings — which source field becomes which target predicate, with its stated relationship, one ConceptMap-shaped table per source and target; representable from and producible as a FHIR ConceptMap.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/vocab-mapping"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#graphTypology/schemas",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "schemas",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "A Subgraph of Node Schemas: files that state the shape other files must have.",
      "conformsTo": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/externalSchema/omg-dmn-1.3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/uml",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "uml",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "UML class diagrams of each named sub-graph a harness declares, derived from the node schemas its graph typologies register — PlantUML and Mermaid from one model.",
      "validatorNotApplicable": "its nodes are `.puml` and `.mmd` — PlantUML and Mermaid source, counted 2026-09-24 as 103 and 101. Not JSON, and `derived` besides, so a finding against one is a finding against the generator; `uml:overview:check` grades their currency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/qa",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "qa",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "QA verdicts and their projections — kg-qa audits, block and translation QA, qa-witness documents for the docs site, the viewer-navbar audit, result roll-ups and test runs; every `$schema` family is named in `nodeSchemas`, which is the list — a count here would be a second one, and it was already wrong by one before `viewer-nav-qa/v1` was added. Generated; never hand-edited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/health",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "health",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "Repository health reports — one `health-report/v1` document per sweep, carrying every check's three-state verdict, the thresholds it applied and the basis each threshold was chosen on. Generated by `test/health/run.ts`; never hand-edited.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/health-report"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/attestations",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#GraphTypology",
      "name": "attestations",
      "renderable": false,
      "summary": "QA attestations — the judgements a QA family carries across runs (pair attestations, voice reviews, agent and human verdicts, bibliography verifications and human reviews), one `qa-attestations/v1` file per subject, mirroring the derived family's tree. Kept on main where deleting derived results cannot reach them; each entry pins the hash it attested, so a stale one is detectable.",
      "validator": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-staging-content-change-review-phases/cat-harness/schema/qa-attestations"
    },
    {
